<title>GERMANY: BOBSLEIGH-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BOBSLEIGH-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>KOENIGSSEE, Germany 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results in</p>
<p>the four-man event at the European bobsleigh championships on</p>
<p>Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Switzerland II (Reto Goetschi/Guido Acklin/Daniel Giger/</p>
<p>Beat Seitz)    1 minute 34.93 seconds (47.33/47.60)</p>
<p>2. Switzerland I (Marcel Rohner/Markus Nuessli/Thomas</p>
<p>Schreiber/Roland Tanner)	1:34.95 (47.33/47.62)</p>
<p>3 equal. Germany I (Harald Czudaj/Torsten Voss/Alexander</p>
<p>Szelig/Udo Lehmann)	     1:35.06 (47.41/47.65)</p>
<p>3 equal. Germany III (Dirk Wiese/Christoph Bartsch/Markus</p>
<p>Zimmermann/Michael Liekmeier) 1:35.06 (47.56/47.50)</p>
<p>5. Germany II (Wolfgang Hoppe/Sven Ruehr/Oliver Felsen/Carsten</p>
<p>Embach) 1:35.13 (47.50/47.63)</p>
<p>6. Austria I (Hubert Schoesser/Gerd Habermueller/Erwin</p>
<p>Arnold/Martin Schuetzenauer) 1:35.26 (47.50/47.76)</p>
<p> 7. Italy I			 1:35.48 (47.62/47.86)</p>
<p> 8. Great Britain I	     1:35.74 (47.75/47.99)</p>
<p>World Cup standings after five events:</p>
<p> 1. Switzerland I		 151 points</p>
<p> 2. Germany II		    146</p>
<p> 3. Italy I			 143</p>
